  "description": "Subject: Configuration Details \u2013 Temperature Sensor (Gateway)\n\nThe device is registered as **Temperature Sensor**, a gateway\u2011class unit (deviceClass = \u201cgateway\u201d) identified by the gateway ID **abcdef1234567890abcdef12**. It operates in a warehouse environment (tag\u202f\u201clocation\u201d:\u202f\u201cwarehouse\u201d, tag\u202f\u201ctype\u201d:\u202f\u201cenvironment\u201d) and has no parent device (parentId is null). Data are sampled every **60** seconds (systemInterval\u202f=\u202f60) and duplicate measurements are not retained (keepDuplicates\u202f=\u202ffalse).\n\nThe sensor reports two attributes. The primary attribute **temperature** is a numeric reading transmitted as **application/json**; its description reads \u201cCurrent temperature reading.\u201d and it carries an attribute tag indicating the unit is **Celsius**. System\u2011level processing aggregates this value using the **MEAN** function; no aggregation options are defined. A child attribute named **temperature_raw** is included under a whitelist rule, limited to the devices with IDs **1234567890abcdef12345678** and **abcdef1234567890abcdef12**. The secondary attribute **status** is a boolean flag indicating the operational status of the sensor, described as \u201cOperational status of the sensor.\u201d",
